WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:16.548
On cold autumn nights, the children gathered around the fireplace in the schoolroom.

2
00:00:18.409 --> 00:00:22.933
They read or played games while snacking on popcorn, nuts, and apples.

3
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:31.500
Their favorite activity was telling stories, but one October evening, they ran out of tales.

4
00:00:33.168 --> 00:00:37.812
"Let's make a rule that the next person who enters the room must tell us a story," Nat

5
00:00:37.872 --> 00:00:41.315
said. "It'll be amusing to see who comes in first!"

6
00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:48.101
The others agreed with eager grins, and soon Jo arrived, looking for something.

7
00:00:49.202 --> 00:00:55.207
The children waited until Jo took a few steps into the room and then pounced on her, demanding

8
00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:55.807
a story.

9
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:04.565
Jo laughed as Dan guided her over to the big chair.

10
00:01:04.585 --> 00:01:10.006
"You sly cats—am I the first story mouse you've caught?"

11
00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:11.247
she asked.

12
00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:14.728
"Yes!" they all said at once.

13
00:01:16.068 --> 00:01:18.649
"Now, what should my story be about?"

14
00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:22.150
"Boys!" the boys shouted.

15
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.290
"A brave girl!"

16
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:25.831
Nan called out.

17
00:01:27.311 --> 00:01:28.932
"Do you have any ideas, Daisy?"

18
00:01:29.332 --> 00:01:33.190
Jo asked kindly, trying to draw her into the conversation.

19
00:01:34.371 --> 00:01:39.455
But Daisy, who'd been very quiet since her father died, just shrugged.

20
00:01:41.196 --> 00:01:45.880
Jo looked back at the other children's excited faces and began her story.

21
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:51.445
"James Snow and his mother were poor and lived in a small house.

22
00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.888
James was supposed to help his mother, but he preferred to read."

23
00:01:55.908 --> 00:01:59.992
"Did James get in trouble for reading too much?"

24
00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:01.152
Nan asked.

25
00:02:02.693 --> 00:02:09.376
"No, in fact, his mother let him read while she did everything around the house," Jo said.

26
00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:16.980
"Oh, that's not right," said Demi, who was quite proud of helping his widowed mother.

27
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.961
Jo continued with her story.

28
00:02:19.981 --> 00:02:27.164
"One autumn James wanted to attend school, but he didn't have money for schoolbooks.

29
00:02:27.184 --> 00:02:35.107
The local minister agreed to help on one condition: James had to fill his mother's woodbox all winter."

30
00:02:35.127 --> 00:02:38.748
"Chopping wood is so easy!"

31
00:02:39.148 --> 00:02:39.808
Dan said.

32
00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:48.131
Jo smiled and went on, "At first it was easy to gather enough wood, but in November, the

33
00:02:48.191 --> 00:02:51.952
weather grew cold, and James' mother burned lots of wood.

34
00:02:53.948 --> 00:02:57.490
At one point she had to spend her own money for more."

35
00:02:58.931 --> 00:03:00.652
"James was in trouble!"

36
00:03:01.072 --> 00:03:02.453
Nan said gleefully.

37
00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:12.659
"Fortunately James realized he needed to work," Jo said, "so he did anything he could to earn money.

38
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:20.464
The minister was so proud of James that he secretly sent a new saw to the boy.

39
00:03:22.088 --> 00:03:27.390
And James was so grateful that he kept his mother's woodbox full all winter.

40
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:28.930
The end."

41
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.891
"Would it help my mother if I cut wood for her?"

42
00:03:33.271 --> 00:03:34.092
Demi asked.

43
00:03:35.432 --> 00:03:40.513
"It might," Jo said as Rob walked into the room, dragging his quilt behind him.

44
00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:46.055
"You're already helping her, Demi, and your father would be proud."

45
00:03:47.415 --> 00:03:49.216
"Mama, I can't sleep!"

46
00:03:49.636 --> 00:03:53.479
Rob said, heading straight for Jo and climbing into her lap.

47
00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:57.923
"You'd better go back to bed, Rob," Jack said.

48
00:03:57.943 --> 00:04:02.807
"Everyone who comes in has to tell a story, and you can't do that."

49
00:04:02.827 --> 00:04:05.729
"Yes, I can!

50
00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:10.313
I tell Teddy lots of stories about bears and moons and talking bugs!"

51
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:16.938
"Tell us one right now," Dan said, prepared to carry Rob back to bed.

52
00:04:16.958 --> 00:04:20.401
"Let me think," Rob said.

53
00:04:20.421 --> 00:04:25.864
"Getting up in the middle of the night runs in this family," Jo mused.

54
00:04:25.884 --> 00:04:30.026
"I was always hopping in and out of bed as a child."

55
00:04:30.046 --> 00:04:32.988
"Demi used to do it too!"

56
00:04:33.548 --> 00:04:36.730
Daisy exclaimed, her face bright with excitement.

57
00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:41.793
Jo glanced at Daisy, delighted to hear her sounding happy.

58
00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:45.795
"Yes, he—" "I've got a story now!"

59
00:04:46.275 --> 00:04:47.136
Rob interrupted.

60
00:04:48.412 --> 00:04:53.395
"Once upon a time, a lady had a million children and one nice little boy.

61
00:04:55.336 --> 00:05:00.219
She told him not to go outside, but he did and fell into the well with a loud

62
00:05:00.279 --> 00:05:05.742
splash." After this startling beginning, Rob paused for breath.

63
00:05:07.203 --> 00:05:08.323
"Is that all?"

64
00:05:08.723 --> 00:05:09.484
Jack asked.

65
00:05:10.965 --> 00:05:11.845
"No, there's more."

66
00:05:12.866 --> 00:05:16.348
Rob wrinkled his brow in concentration for a few seconds.

67
00:05:18.812 --> 00:05:21.473
"What did the lady do when the boy fell into the well?"

68
00:05:21.973 --> 00:05:23.194
Jo prompted her son.

69
00:05:23.214 --> 00:05:29.677
"She used the bucket to get him out, and then she wrapped him in newspaper and put him

70
00:05:29.857 --> 00:05:32.858
on a shelf to dry, like a seed drying out."

71
00:05:35.379 --> 00:05:42.022
Everyone laughed at this silly story, with Daisy adding, "That's how I dried my flower seeds."

72
00:05:43.562 --> 00:05:50.097
"Exactly! And now it's time for bed," Jo said, scooping up Rob and making her escape.

73
00:05:50.117 --> 00:05:57.261
"I wonder who'll come in next," said Daisy, who was beginning to enjoy herself.

74
00:05:58.722 --> 00:06:07.467
When they heard footsteps in the hall, Nan ran to the door and cried, "Asia, come in!"

75
00:06:07.487 --> 00:06:08.528
"No, no!"

76
00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:12.950
Asia laughed and was careful to stay in the hall.

77
00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:16.152
"Mrs. Bauer warned me!"

78
00:06:17.308 --> 00:06:22.830
So Asia managed to avoid the children, but they soon heard someone new humming.

79
00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:25.570
"It's Mr.

80
00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:31.692
Bauer!" Tommy said, "and if we laugh loudly, he'll wonder what the joke is."

81
00:06:35.473 --> 00:06:42.015
Sure enough, the professor couldn't resist the sound of laughter—especially since some of it was coming from Demi

82
00:06:42.155 --> 00:06:42.795
and Daisy.

83
00:06:42.815 --> 00:06:44.836
"What's going on?"

84
00:06:45.296 --> 00:06:48.302
he said, walking right into the children's trap.

85
00:06:49.383 --> 00:06:51.064
"You're telling us a story!"

86
00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:55.107
Dan explained their game and led him to the storyteller's chair.

87
00:06:57.109 --> 00:07:02.293
The professor thought for a moment and then told a story about Grandpa March and a robber.

88
00:07:03.594 --> 00:07:08.558
After Grandpa March was kind to him, the robber didn't have the heart to take any money.

89
00:07:08.578 --> 00:07:12.361
"That was a short story—tell us another one!"

90
00:07:12.822 --> 00:07:13.722
Nat complained.

91
00:07:13.742 --> 00:07:20.523
"No, too many stories are as bad as too many cookies," the professor said.

92
00:07:21.503 --> 00:07:24.725
He jumped up and ran down the hall with everyone chasing him.

93
00:07:26.907 --> 00:07:30.629
However, he had a good head start and safely reached his study.

94
00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:32.931
"Good night, everyone!"

95
00:07:33.371 --> 00:07:34.892
he called through the closed door.
